---
import Work from "@layouts/Work.astro";

export const frontmatter = {
    title: "Death and Revival",
    date: "2022.12.09",
    coverImage: "/deathandrevival/Church 2.jpg",
};
---

<Work
    title={frontmatter.title}
    subtitle="A Study of Bodies, Cities, and Cycles of Change"
    description="Architectural studio project exploring the relationship between human bodies, urban environments, and the cyclical nature of change. The research examines three temporal states—present, death, and revival—juxtaposing the idealized forms of Renaissance architecture with the evolving realities of both body and city. Through this lens, the project reflects on how perfection is not a fixed condition but a cycle of decline, adaptation, and renewal."
    coverImage={frontmatter.coverImage}
    coverImageAlt={frontmatter.title}
    course="Architectural Studio VI"
    courseDescription="Radicle Roots"
    advisor="Christianna Bennett"
    collaborators="Marinie Ben"
    date={frontmatter.date}
    location="Rome, Italy"
    gallery={import.meta.glob("/public/deathandrevival/gallery/*")}
>
    <section class="stack">
        <p>
            Renaissance architecture reflects an idealized vision of the human
            body—proportioned, perfected, and measured against classical notions
            of harmony. Yet the human body is never static; it adapts to its
            environment just as landscapes shift under natural forces and
            cultural change. This project examines adaptation across three
            temporal states — present, death, and revival — juxtaposing the
            Renaissance pursuit of perfection with the evolving realities of
            both body and architecture.
        </p>
        <p>
            In the present, human life is abundant, and the city mirrors its
            disparities. Wealthier districts expand outward with access to
            diverse ecological systems, while poorer areas compress into dense,
            survival-driven conditions. At death, population and pollution reach
            their peak. The world becomes a fractured, artificial landscape
            stripped of nature, where social structures collapse into pack
            mentalities and outsiders fend for themselves. In revival, the
            environment begins to heal. Organic matter reclaims the artificial,
            ecosystems regenerate, and life gradually returns.
        </p>
        <p>
            Across these three states, the project reflects on how bodies,
            cities, and architectural ideals transform under pressure —
            revealing that perfection is not a fixed condition, but a cycle of
            decline, adaptation, and renewal.
        </p>
    </section>

    <img
        src="/deathandrevival/Preliminary Studies.jpg"
        alt="Preliminary Studies"
    />

    <section class="stack">
        <h3>Object Study</h3>
        <p>
            These three forms establish the project's conceptual spectrum:
            idealized human → distorted human → non-human organic. They become
            the basis for understanding how architecture shifts across present,
            death, and revival.
        </p>

        <div class="grid auto-fit">
            <div class="stack">
                <h4 class="center">Object 1</h4>
                <h5 class="center">Organic Mis-Figured Human Head</h5>
                <p>
                    An irregular, distorted human head represents the body as it
                    exists in reality — imperfect, adaptive, and shaped by
                    external forces. Its organic asymmetry becomes a
                    counterpoint to Renaissance ideals.
                </p>
            </div>
            <img
                class="full-height"
                src="/deathandrevival/Organic Head 1.jpg"
                alt="Organic Head 1"
            />
            <div class="grid col-2 auto-rows">
                <img
                    class="full-height"
                    src="/deathandrevival/Organic Head 2.jpg"
                    alt="Organic Head 2"
                />
                <img
                    class="full-height"
                    src="/deathandrevival/Organic Head Texture.jpg"
                    alt="Organic Head Texture"
                />
                <img
                    class="full-height"
                    src="/deathandrevival/Organic Head 3.jpg"
                    alt="Organic Head 3"
                />
                <img
                    class="full-height"
                    src="/deathandrevival/Organic Head 4.jpg"
                    alt="Organic Head 4"
                />
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="grid auto-fit">
            <div class="stack">
                <h4 class="center">Object 2</h4>
                <h5 class="center">Artificial Perfect Human Head</h5>
                <p>
                    A geometrically idealized head reflects the Renaissance
                    pursuit of proportion and harmony. Its artificial precision
                    embodies the cultural desire to standardize and perfect the
                    human form.
                </p>
            </div>
            <img
                class="full-height"
                src="/deathandrevival/Artificial Head 1.jpg"
                alt="Artificial Head 1"
            />
            <div class="grid col-2 auto-rows">
                <img
                    src="/deathandrevival/Artificial Head 2.jpg"
                    alt="Artificial Head 2"
                />
                <img
                    src="/deathandrevival/Artificial Head Texture.jpg"
                    alt="Artificial Head Texture"
                />
                <img
                    src="/deathandrevival/Artificial Head 3.jpg"
                    alt="Artificial Head 3"
                />
                <img
                    src="/deathandrevival/Artificial Head 4.jpg"
                    alt="Artificial Head 4"
                />
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="grid auto-fit">
            <div class="stack">
                <h4 class="center">Object 3</h4>
                <h5 class="center">Organic Unliving Rock</h5>
                <p>
                    A natural rock form introduces a third condition: organic
                    matter without life. Its irregular geometry becomes a
                    reference for the revival state, where nature reclaims the
                    artificial.
                </p>
            </div>
            <img
                class="full-height"
                src="/deathandrevival/Rock 1.jpg"
                alt="Rock 1"
            />
            <div class="stack">
                <div class="row">
                    <img
                        class="half-width full-height"
                        src="/deathandrevival/Rock 2.jpg"
                        alt="Rock 2"
                    />
                    <img
                        class="half-width full-height"
                        src="/deathandrevival/Rock Texture.jpg"
                        alt="Rock Texture"
                    />
                </div>
                <div class="row">
                    <img
                        class="full-height"
                        src="/deathandrevival/Rock 3.jpg"
                        alt="Rock 3"
                    />
                    <img
                        class="full-height"
                        src="/deathandrevival/Rock 4.jpg"
                        alt="Rock 4"
                    />
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="stack">
        <h3>Texture Study</h3>
        <p>
            These textures visualize how landscape shifts from strained →
            artificial → reclaimed, mirroring the project's temporal arc.
        </p>

        <div class="grid auto-fit">
            <div class="stack">
                <h4 class="center">Texture 1</h4>
                <h5 class="center">Goo-Like Exterior Landscape</h5>
                <p>
                    A viscous, unstable surface represents the present state,
                    where ecological systems are strained and landscapes begin
                    to deform under human pressure.
                </p>
            </div>
            <img
                src="/deathandrevival/Preliminary Studies.jpg"
                alt="Preliminary Studies"
            />
            <div class="stack">
                <div class="row">
                    <img
                        src="/deathandrevival/Preliminary Studies.jpg"
                        alt="Preliminary Studies"
                    />
                    <img
                        src="/deathandrevival/Preliminary Studies.jpg"
                        alt="Preliminary Studies"
                    />
                </div>
                <div class="row">
                    <img
                        src="/deathandrevival/Preliminary Studies.jpg"
                        alt="Preliminary Studies"
                    />
                    <img
                        src="/deathandrevival/Preliminary Studies.jpg"
                        alt="Preliminary Studies"
                    />
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="grid auto-fit">
            <div class="stack">
                <h4 class="center">Texture 2</h4>
                <h5 class="center">Artificial Labyrinth (Uniform Growth)</h5>
                <p>
                    A partially developed labyrinth with identical hedge growth
                    reflects the death state: artificial order imposed on
                    nature, uniformity replacing organic variation.
                </p>
            </div>
            <img
                src="/deathandrevival/Preliminary Studies.jpg"
                alt="Preliminary Studies"
            />
            <div class="stack">
                <div class="row">
                    <img
                        src="/deathandrevival/Preliminary Studies.jpg"
                        alt="Preliminary Studies"
                    />
                    <img
                        src="/deathandrevival/Preliminary Studies.jpg"
                        alt="Preliminary Studies"
                    />
                </div>
                <div class="row">
                    <img
                        src="/deathandrevival/Preliminary Studies.jpg"
                        alt="Preliminary Studies"
                    />
                    <img
                        src="/deathandrevival/Preliminary Studies.jpg"
                        alt="Preliminary Studies"
                    />
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="grid auto-fit">
            <div class="stack">
                <h4 class="center">Texture 3</h4>
                <h5 class="center">Organic Labyrinth (Irregular Growth)</h5>
                <p>
                    A fully developed labyrinth with uneven, organic hedge
                    growth represents revival. Nature reasserts itself, breaking
                    the artificial grid and restoring complexity.
                </p>
            </div>
            <img
                src="/deathandrevival/Preliminary Studies.jpg"
                alt="Preliminary Studies"
            />
            <div class="stack">
                <div class="row">
                    <img
                        src="/deathandrevival/Preliminary Studies.jpg"
                        alt="Preliminary Studies"
                    />
                    <img
                        src="/deathandrevival/Preliminary Studies.jpg"
                        alt="Preliminary Studies"
                    />
                </div>
                <div class="row">
                    <img
                        src="/deathandrevival/Preliminary Studies.jpg"
                        alt="Preliminary Studies"
                    />
                    <img
                        src="/deathandrevival/Preliminary Studies.jpg"
                        alt="Preliminary Studies"
                    />
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="stack">
        <h3>Concept</h3>
        <p>
            The grid and the church establish the architectural framework that
            persists through present, death, and revival, allowing the landscape
            and textures to transform around a stable core.
        </p>

        <div class="row relaxed">
            <div class="stack">
                <h4>Inspiration: Modern Grid Interpretation</h4>
                <p>
                    A modern take on the classic principles of architecture
                    demonstrated through gridlike structures
                </p>
                <p>
                    The project reinterprets classical architectural principles
                    through a modern grid system. The grid becomes a structural
                    and organizational tool that adapts across the three
                    temporal states, shifting from rigid order to fractured
                    geometry to organic reclamation.
                </p>
                <img src="/deathandrevival/Inspiration.png" alt="Inspiration" />
            </div>
            <div class="stack">
                <h4>Focus: Preservation of the Monumental Church</h4>
                <p>
                    Preservation of the classic monumental church maintained
                    through its use as a public gathering space
                </p>
                <p>
                    A Renaissance church remains the central anchor throughout
                    all states. Its monumental form persists as a public
                    gathering space, even as the surrounding landscape
                    transforms. The church becomes a constant against which the
                    changing environment is measured.
                </p>
                <img src="/deathandrevival/Focus.png" alt="Focus" />
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section id="timeline" class="stack">
        <div class="stack tight slider">
            <div class="row labels">
                <h3>Present</h3>
                <h3>Death</h3>
                <h3>Revival</h3>
            </div>
            <input type="range" min="0" max="2" step="0.02" value="0" />
        </div>
        <div class="stack">
            <div class="image">
                <img
                    src="/deathandrevival/Plan 0.png"
                    data-index="0"
                    alt="Plan 0"
                />
                <img
                    src="/deathandrevival/Plan 1.png"
                    data-index="1"
                    alt="Plan 1"
                />
                <img
                    src="/deathandrevival/Plan 2.png"
                    data-index="2"
                    alt="Plan 2"
                />
            </div>
            <div class="image">
                <img
                    src="/deathandrevival/Section 0.png"
                    data-index="0"
                    alt="Section"
                />
                <img
                    src="/deathandrevival/Section 1.png"
                    data-index="1"
                    alt="Section"
                />
                <img
                    src="/deathandrevival/Section 2.png"
                    data-index="2"
                    alt="Section"
                />
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
    <script src="../../scripts/timeline.js"></script>
</Work>

<style>
    #timeline {
        align-items: center;
        max-height: calc(
            var(--window-height) - var(--hScrollbarSize) - (2 * var(--gap))
        );
    }

    #timeline > * {
        width: 100%;
    }

    #timeline :last-child {
        overflow: hidden;
    }

    #timeline > * > * {
        justify-content: space-between;
    }

    #timeline h3 {
        opacity: 0.4;
    }

    #timeline h3.active {
        opacity: 1;
    }

    #timeline .image {
        position: relative;
        background-color: var(--color-bg);
        overflow: hidden;
    }

    #timeline img {
        position: absolute;
        top: 0;
        opacity: 0;
    }
</style>
